{#-
  CowSwap Milkman — submit price-protected swap orders.

  Uses the Chainlink DynamicSlippageChecker (aliases.curator.price_checker) as the
  pinned price checker. Its priceCheckerData is ABI-encoded as
  (uint256 slippageBps, bytes innerData), where innerData is itself
  abi.encode(address[] feeds, bool[] reverses) — the price oracle the slippage
  check measures the swap against. The policy bounds slippageBps per pair AND
  pins innerData to the exact feed configuration for the pair.

  Pinning innerData is load-bearing, not cosmetic: the slippage cap is a bound
  relative to whatever price the feeds report. If innerData were left free, a
  compromised role member could supply a feed reporting a fair price of ~0, so
  "lose no more than slippageBps" would permit swapping the Safe's tokens for
  ~nothing and still clear the gate. Nothing downstream (Milkman, the checker,
  its calculator) restricts the feed addresses, so the policy must.

  Required params:
    pairs — list of allowed swaps, each with its own slippage cap and the exact
            Chainlink feed path used to price it:
              - from: <TOKEN key>              # token the Safe swaps from
                to: <TOKEN key>                # token the Safe receives
                max_slippage_bps: <int>        # UNQUOTED integer; e.g. 500 ≡ ≤ 5%
                feeds: [<feed addr>, ...]      # the price path, in order
                reverses: [<bool>, ...]        # one per feed; same length
            feeds/reverses must equal exactly what the swap submits for this
            pair (see RequestMilkmanSwap): the path starts at the `from` token's
            feed and ends at the `to` token's feed, reversed. USDC → PYUSD uses
            feeds: [USDC/USD, PYUSD/USD], reverses: [false, true]; PYUSD → USDC
            uses feeds: [PYUSD/USD, USDC/USD], reverses: [false, true]. The path
            depends on both ends of the pair, which is why each pair carries its
            own. One `or` branch per pair, with the cap and feeds bound to it.
            (A single resulting branch collapses to a plain match — no redundant
            `or`.)

  Optional params:
    max_approval — exclusive upper bound (in base units) for the approve `amount`
                   on every from-token, emitted as `less_than max_approval`.
                   Defaults to uint256.max, which only rules out the literal
                   infinite-approval sentinel and does NOT bound exposure. Set it to
                   a realistic operational ceiling to cap how much the role can
                   approve to Milkman in one shot. A single value applies to all
                   from-tokens, so it is most precise with one from-token; with
                   mixed decimals, pick a bound valid for each.

  Policy enforced:
    approve(spender=Milkman, amount < max_approval) on each distinct `from` token.
      Pinning the spender prevents approving arbitrary contracts. The amount bound
      is an EXCLUSIVE ceiling: by default it is uint256.max, which only excludes the
      infinite-approval sentinel — it does NOT limit exposure (any amount below it,
      up to the whole Safe balance, is allowed, and `amountIn` on the swap is `pass`).
      Set `max_approval` to a realistic ceiling to bound standing/per-swap exposure.
    requestSwapExactTokensForTokens, per pair branch:
      amountIn     pass
      fromToken    == aliases.tokens[pair.from]
      toToken      == aliases.tokens[pair.to]
      to           == avatar (proceeds stay in the Safe)
      appData      pass (CoW Protocol order metadata, set at runtime)
      priceChecker == aliases.curator.price_checker (Chainlink DynamicSlippageChecker)
      priceCheckerData → abi_encoded:
        slippageBps  < pair.max_slippage_bps + 1   (i.e. ≤ pair.max_slippage_bps)
        innerData    == abi.encode(pair.feeds, pair.reverses)
                                                  (the feed path is pinned, so the
                                                   cap is measured against a fixed
                                                   oracle, not a caller-chosen one)

    Note: cancelSwap is NOT included. Milkman's cancelSwap targets the per-swap
    order clone (address unknown at policy-creation time), so it cannot be
    pre-authorised; cancellations are executed directly through the Safe UI.
-#}
{#- Fail fast on malformed pairs: emitting an undefined variable throws under
    throwOnUndefined, pointing at the offending guard line. -#}
{%- if pairs is not defined or (pairs | length) == 0 -%}
  {{ milkman_error_pairs_must_be_a_non_empty_list }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- for pair in pairs -%}
  {%- set pair_index = loop.index0 -%}
  {%- if pair.from == pair.to -%}
    {{ milkman_error_pair_from_and_to_must_differ }}
  {%- endif -%}
  {#- Must be an UNQUOTED integer: nunjucks `+` concatenates strings, so a
      quoted "200" would render the less_than ceiling as "2001" (a 10× more
      permissive cap), and a missing value would render NaN. -#}
  {%- if pair.max_slippage_bps is not number -%}
    {{ milkman_error_max_slippage_bps_must_be_an_unquoted_integer }}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if pair.feeds is not defined or pair.reverses is not defined
        or (pair.feeds | length) == 0 or (pair.feeds | length) != (pair.reverses | length) -%}
    {{ milkman_error_feeds_and_reverses_must_be_non_empty_and_of_equal_length }}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- for other in pairs -%}
    {%- if loop.index0 > pair_index and other.from == pair.from and other.to == pair.to -%}
      {{ milkman_error_duplicate_pair }}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{#- Deduplicate the from-token keys for the approves, in order of first use. -#}
{%- set from_keys = [] -%}
{%- for pair in pairs -%}
  {%- if pair.from not in from_keys -%}
    {%- set _ = from_keys.push(pair.from) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
roles:
{%- for token in from_keys %}
  - address: "{{ aliases.tokens[token] }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function approve(address spender, uint256 amount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: spender
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ aliases.curator.milkman }}"
            value_type: "address"
          - name: amount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "less_than"
            value: "{{ max_approval | default('115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639935') }}"
            value_type: "uint256"
{%- endfor %}

  - address: "{{ aliases.curator.milkman }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function requestSwapExactTokensForTokens(uint256 amountIn, address fromToken, address toToken, address to, bytes32 appData, address priceChecker, bytes priceCheckerData)"
        execution_options: "none"
        operator: "or"
        branches:
{%- for pair in pairs %}
          - operator: "matches"
            params:
              - name: amountIn
                operator: "pass"
              - name: fromToken
                operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ aliases.tokens[pair.from] }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - name: toToken
                operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ aliases.tokens[pair.to] }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - name: to
                operator: "equal_to_avatar"
              - name: appData
                operator: "pass"
              - name: priceChecker
                operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ aliases.curator.price_checker }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - name: priceCheckerData
                param_type: "abi_encoded"
                children:
                  - name: slippageBps
                    param_type: "static"
                    operator: "less_than"
                    value: "{{ pair.max_slippage_bps + 1 }}"
                    value_type: "uint256"
                  - name: innerData
                    param_type: "dynamic"
                    operator: "equal_to"
                    value: "{{ [pair.feeds, pair.reverses] | abi_encode(['address[]', 'bool[]']) }}"
                    value_type: "bytes"
                    # display-only: lets `zac plan` decode the pinned blob back to
                    # (feeds, reverses) instead of printing opaque hex.
                    display_decode:
                      - { name: feeds, type: "address[]" }
                      - { name: reverses, type: "bool[]" }
{%- endfor %}
